[S] YAAP Lupus: Rog-Lyc

Upon entering the dungeon you have 3 problems to solve: hunger, weight and
uncontrolled lycanthropsy.  The first is the result of your regeneration
(which makes you pretty good in combat).  The second is the result of the
third.  You spend 98% of your time as a wolf until you find a way to
control it.  And there's really only one way.  Unlike Doppelgangers you
don't solve it by hitting level 7.  You must find a ring of poly control.

Until you find the ring you go around as a wolf with a carrying capacity
of under 300 (unless your Str and Con is good, which mine never were).
So not only can't you wear any of the cool stuff you find in the dungeon
(since you're a wolf) you can't even lug it around until you can.  And
when your wolf hitpoints (which are often pretty meager) evaporate you
turn into a naked human with no weapon in hand.  Needless to say this
makes the Rogue class, and his host of daggers a good choice.

Being able to summon wolves and winter wolves is great for defense, but
terrible if you want to manage your hunger.  Praying becomes a common
resort to fill your bottomless stomach.

This all being the case I regularly clear out the mines and finish Sobokan
before I run into real problems with being in wolf form all the time.
When you hit lvl 9 and Dlvl 10 you start to encounter some pretty
dangerous monsters that are hard to beat.  Especially hard is getting a
form of MR and Reflection that your wolf-form can use.

So, while I always play wishless that conduct just wouldn't cut it for a
Lyc.  The odds of finding a =PC are really really low.  You have a much
better chance of finding a wish via wand, fountain, or magic lamp.

I started this game with the pistol and bad stats.  The pistol meant I'd
have to find a dagger to start practicing so my human form wouldn't be
completely defenseless.  The bad stats means I could only carry about 200.
So I drop most of my starting eq except for the lock pick (which I can't
use as a wolf) the bag (which I'll have to drop soon).  I start quaffing
all the fountains I see and quickly get See Invisibility.  No wishes
though.

I hit the mall first, there's a bones file and I need to fight off some
dangerous baddies before I can check the stores.  Using the stairs as a
retreat I dispatch the foes.  No magic lamp in the shop. Nothing
particularly good in the other shops.  I rack up some credit in the
general store with the help of my wolves, then down to sobokan.

Pick up all the rings and wands.  One of the worst parts of being a Lyc is
that when your stats improve while you're in wolf form they don't carry
over to Human form.  This means it's probably better to do sobokan after
you find your PC.  But I always try to find my ring before resorting to a
wish. [S] sobokan has some interesting new puzzles.  I hit a few I haven't
seen before this time around.  It takes away a lot of the bordome.  I
foudn one level with lava inside, and another with 2 paths to the stairs.
At the top was the BoH, which isn't my first choice, since i already had a
Oilskin Bag and just needed a !oGL to make it into BoH.  Besides it means
that my wolf form probably would never get reflection.

I check out all the rings by price at the shop, nothing.  So down to the
mines I go.

The minetown shop has a magic candle but no magic lamp.  I get really
repressed, cry, sob, that this character will not go far then I steal the
candle with the help of my wolves.  I rack up some more credit at the
local stores.  The altar is co-aligned.  But it doesn't do much good since
getting the Bat From Hell just means I have to lug around 20 more and hope
no one else gets a hold of it when I drop it.

I decide to do the rest of the mines.  The bottom is the holy-water
factory.  I hit a few poly traps and become a Fire Vampire (which is
pretty darn cool).  They make peaceful anyone you hit.  Very nice.  So I
clear out the mines in that form, and go back up to Mineown.  For some
reason I check out the lamp shop again and lo-an-behold, a magic lamp!
And hey, it's blessed.  Not sure how I missed it before.

Rub rub rub.  blessed ring of polymorphy control, please.

Okay, so now I sac and get the Bat From Hell (probably the best single
artifact weapon in [S]).  I also found some bones of a wizard and got
Magicbane and a CoMR.  Things were starting to look up.  After this point
you're basically playing a normal human with one less ring finger and
constant annoyance from "Do you want tranform into a wolf? (y/n)".  The
worst part about this is that and using VI keys is that upper left
diagonal is "y".  So sometimes you fall out of your armor into wolf form
at the worst times.

Below the oracle I found GoP, turned some elf mithral into Dark Elf
mithral.  Found a altar on Dlvl 16 and made it base camp.

After this there are only a few things of interest.  After I enchanted up
a T-Shirt to +5 I lost it in the Quest when I polied into a Xorn and took
everything off but the shirt: Rip.  After I enchanted up my +4GoP and +4
Helm of Telepathy I lost them both to a Ghoul Mage in Moloch's Temple
while I was in Xorn form (and thus w/o MR) because I forgot Ls aren't the
only casters to watch out for.  So in about 30mins of playing I went from
-38AC to -20AC or something like that.

A paucity of magic markers (only one that i used on all the stuff gone)
and enchant armor scrolls let me to have a very high AC for most of the
late game.  I compensated by having a sac fest at an altar on Dlvl 33.  I
don't normally pray/sac so this was new and interesting for me.

I met some new friends the Steel Golum that has a disenchantment attack,
and the Mingo Queen(?) that has a mind flayer attack.  I really suffered a
lot of stupidity attacks during this game.  I didn't know about the mingo
queen until my Int was 8.  And later I got hit with a !ofAmnesia.  I must
have mapped out the dungeon by foot 4 times total.  Never did find Ludios.

The last bit of fun happened with Demogorgon.  I always try to do things
differently each time I meet him.  I've gone toe-to-toe (I'm 1 for 2),
and I've stoned him with a *tice corpse so far.  This time I tried to get
fancy.  Since this game revolved so much around having PC I decided to
make it my method of attack.  The plan was to 1) poly into a basilisk,
2) teleport down, 3) quaff an invulnerability potion, 4) let him hit me
and stone himself.  Unfortuantely, I forgot about step 3.  Demo decided to
hit me with a psy-blast for 140HP of damage (basilisks don't have much
more than 50HP).  So I reverted into human form, got stung, got stung, got
stung.  I had some !oFH so I quaffed and got stung some more before I got
a turn in.  I was only fast, since basilisks can't wear boots.  When got
my turn I dropped a scroll of scarey monster (I don't believe in Elbereth,
but do like the scroll). I turned into a basilisk again, quaffed my
invulnerability potion and stepped off the scroll.  Worked like it should
have the first time.  [if you want to see this part of the mis-adventure
it is saved on the antisymmetric server - load game ttick_Lyc_DemoClose]

My AK was missing one item, =FreeAction.  Thanks for people in this forum
for setting me straigh on why I didn't really need it.  I was under the
impression that MR didn't prevent me from being held by priest spells.

On Astral my only concern was Pestilence.  But the two altars guarded by
his buddies weren't what I wanted.  So I had to face Pesty.  And sure
enough I walked in the door and Pesty hits me a few times.  I quaff.  Then
a priest throws a !ofParalysis at me (my worst fear since no =FA).  I
probably ended the paralysis with 1 turn to cure my illness.  After that I
just teleported everyone out of the way and ran for the altar.

